# PROPOSAL, not policy and not a dump. Task 1 speed, step 1 (2026-10-12).
# Load in QGC (Parameters > Tools > Load from file) or type the five values by hand.
# Evidence: lake log 00000045.BIN, runs at 14:40 / 14:56 / 15:07 PDT, 190-239 s for 70-73 m.
#
# WP_PIVOT_ANGLE 30 -> 60  Omni frames pivot (Rover.cpp passes have_skid_steering(), true
#                          for omni), and GUIDED re-checks the pivot on EVERY setpoint we
#                          stream. Each pivot brakes desired speed to 0. That happened 40-52%
#                          of every lake run, the main time sink. Try 0 (off) if 60 still shows it.
# WP_SPEED      3.0 -> 1.0  Top speed measured 1.25-1.33 m/s at ~100% throttle. A cap near it
#                          leaves no thrust headroom for yaw on a 4-thruster omni. 1.0 also
#                          equals the baseline and hs_wp_speed_mps, so check_config stays green.
# CRUISE_SPEED  2.0 -> 1.0  Throttle feed-forward was 15% at 2 m/s. Manual runs needed 52-57%
# CRUISE_THROTTLE 15 -> 55  for 1.0 m/s, so commanded 1.0 m/s delivered ~0.7 m/s.
# WP_JERK       5 (keep)   With ATC_ACCEL_MAX 1, the 2.5 m lookahead allows ~1.5 m/s, so it
#                          is not the limit. WP_ACCEL 2 is inert: min(WP_ACCEL, ATC_ACCEL_MAX).
2	1	WP_PIVOT_ANGLE	60	4
2	1	WP_SPEED	1.0	9
2	1	CRUISE_SPEED	1.0	9
2	1	CRUISE_THROTTLE	55	2
2	1	WP_JERK	5.0	9
